{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be your doctor during this stay. You're here because of abdominal pain, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s the same kind of pain I’ve had before with pancreatitis. It started two nights ago—epigastric, radiating to my back, really sharp."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you’ve been vomiting too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, non-stop since it started. Now it’s just dry heaving. I can’t keep anything down, not even my meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll keep you NPO for now—no food or drink by mouth—to let your pancreas rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. But I did manage to take my Coumadin and lisinopril earlier. Should I keep trying?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, don’t try to take anything by mouth right now. We’ll give your meds through your IV or J-tube if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. My port was placed a few days ago—right side chest. It’s not painful or red."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good, I see the site—it looks clean. We’ll use that for your IV meds and labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had over 30 admissions for this. Is this another flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it looks like an acute flare of your chronic pancreatitis. Your lipase is normal, but your symptoms and history are classic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my triglycerides? I know they were high last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’re elevated at 414, which can contribute to flares. But no imaging is needed—we’re managing based on your typical pattern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about pain control? I need something strong."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting your usual IV regimen: Dilaudid every two hours, Ketorolac, and Phenergan for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. And fluids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, IV fluids at 125 mL/hour to keep you hydrated while you’re NPO."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My blood pressure’s been high. Is that a concern?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s 176/114 now—likely due to pain. We’ve held your lisinopril since you’re not eating, but we’ll restart it when you can take pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my Coumadin? I’m on it for DVT history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR was low at 1.1 on admission, so we’ve started Lovenox injections to bridge you until you can take Coumadin again safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I understand. I’ve had clots before—left arm and now right IJ."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2149-11-16 16:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and with your port and history, we’ll keep you on anticoagulation long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2149-11-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2149-11-17 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. Still nauseous, but not vomiting as much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2149-11-17 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. We’ll keep you NPO a bit longer, but we’ll start advancing your diet tomorrow if you keep improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2149-11-17 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have ice chips or water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2149-11-17 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We want to be sure your gut is ready. We’ll try clear liquids tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2149-11-17 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My blood pressure still high?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2149-11-17 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s coming down—158/98 this morning. As your pain improves, it should normalize."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2149-11-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re going to try clear liquids today—start with broth and apple juice."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2149-11-18 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great! Can I also restart my amitriptyline and methadone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2149-11-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll restart those by mouth. We’ve increased your lisinopril to 40 mg daily for now to help with BP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2149-11-18 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why increase it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2149-11-18 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because your BP has been persistently elevated. We’ll lower it back to 10 mg once it’s stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2149-11-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You tolerated the clear liquids. Today, we’ll advance to soft foods—mashed potatoes, applesauce."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2149-11-19 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. And my Coumadin? Can I restart it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2149-11-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re restarting it today. You’ll stay on both Coumadin and Lovenox until your INR is therapeutic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2149-11-19 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s my INR today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2149-11-19 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s 1.6—still subtherapeutic. We’ll check again in two days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2149-11-20 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re eating regular food now and pain is much better. We’re switching your pain meds to oral Dilaudid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2149-11-20 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I take it as needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2149-11-20 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, one tablet every three hours as needed. We’ll send some home with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2149-11-20 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my amitriptyline? I was on 25 mg at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2149-11-20 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve increased it to 75 mg nightly. It helps with nerve pain and mood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2149-11-21 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is still 1.6. We’re adjusting your Coumadin dose to 7.5 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2149-11-21 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I keep the Lovenox too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2149-11-21 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, once daily 100 mg until your INR is above 2 for 24 hours. Then you can stop the shots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2149-11-21 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And when do I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2149-11-21 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If all goes well, probably in two to three days. We’ll check your labs tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2149-11-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs look stable. Pain is controlled, you’re eating well. We’re planning discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2149-11-22 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What about my meds at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2149-11-22 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home on your regular meds. Coumadin at 7.5 mg daily, Lovenox once a day until your INR is therapeutic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2149-11-22 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the dose change?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2149-11-22 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take 10 mg tonight, then 7.5 mg daily after that. Your INR needs to be checked soon after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2149-11-22 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And lisinopril?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2149-11-22 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Back to your usual 10 mg daily. Your BP is much better—145/99 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2149-11-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge tomorrow. You’re doing really well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2149-11-23 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can someone help me with the Lovenox injections at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2149-11-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, a nurse will come to your home to assist until your INR is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2149-11-23 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2149-11-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your primary doctor and the anticoagulation clinic. They’ll manage your INR checks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Keep taking your meds as discussed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So, Coumadin 10 mg tonight, then 7.5 mg daily, and Lovenox until INR is good?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And call if you have severe pain, vomiting, or signs of bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—my anemia. Labs were low again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your hemoglobin is 9.3. It’s likely anemia of chronic disease from your pancreatitis. No transfusion needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I take iron?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. Your levels are stable. We’ll monitor it at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my migraines?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can resume your butalbital as needed. Avoid triggers and keep a headache diary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been anxious this stay. Any advice?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking your amitriptyline. It helps with both pain and mood. Consider talking to a counselor if anxiety worsens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Just take it slow at home and call with any concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge team will bring your prescriptions and instructions shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll pack up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you in the clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2149-11-24 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll be in touch with your PCP to coordinate care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2149-11-16 16:30:00",
    "admission_end": "2149-11-24 13:41:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for an acute flare of chronic pancreatitis, presenting with severe epigastric abdominal pain radiating to the back, nausea, and persistent vomiting. She was managed with NPO status, IV fluids, and her standard IV pain and anti-nausea regimen, including Dilaudid, Ketorolac, Phenergan, and Ondansetron. Her pain gradually improved, and she was advanced from NPO to clear liquids, then to a regular diet. She restarted her home oral medications, including methadone, amitriptyline, and lisinopril, with a temporary increase in lisinopril dose for blood pressure control. Due to subtherapeutic INR on admission, she was bridged with daily Lovenox while restarting Coumadin, with discharge instructions to take 10 mg Coumadin on the evening of discharge, then 7.5 mg daily, continuing Lovenox until INR was therapeutic for over 24 hours. Her J-tube and port site remained clean, and she remained ambulatory throughout. She was discharged home with home health support for anticoagulation management and follow-up arranged.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute pancreatitis",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Chronic venous embolism and thrombosis of internal jugular veins",
      "Anemia of other chronic disease",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Dysthymic disorder",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants"
    ]
  }
}
